<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Metlife lifts H1 shr, upbeat for year.</title>
<headline>Metlife lifts H1 shr, upbeat for year.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		  9.75	  vs   7.80</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)	6.50	  vs   5.15</p>
<p>    Attrib surplus	  67.3	   vs  54.0</p>
<p>    Recurring premium  1,018.0	   vs  844.0</p>
<p>    Single premiums	136.0	   vs  109.0</p>
<p>    Investment income    364.0	   vs  326.0</p>
<p>Div payable June 27</p>
<p>On register June 13</p>
<p>Full name -  Metropolitan Life Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The life insurance group said it expected premium income, earnings and dividends would show a significant increase for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
